branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie (deployed via deploy branch)
notesT: FIX — the recorded .mp4 sounded higher and restless compared to what you heard
  live ("das Ergebnis klingt anders als während der Session"). Cause: the master-mix
  ring buffer was hard-wired to 48 kHz, but with the rPPG camera active iOS runs the
  audio route at 44.1 kHz — so the captured audio was saved with the wrong rate stamp and
  played back ~9% too fast (higher pitch + off timing). It now uses the REAL capture rate
  for the file and all frame math, so the exported audio matches the live sound.
  Everything else from 10.77 stands: fullscreen immersive visual → Record (top bar, turns
  red) → play music/bio → Stop → share the .mp4 (Metal visual + master-mix audio). Record
  no longer crashes (the 2092 _isInput crash was fixed — audio now comes from the read-only
  RetroCapture ring, no illegal outputNode tap).
  KNOWN LIMITS: A/V sync is best-effort; only the Metal visual records (not the spectrum
  donut); no trim UI yet.
  Test 10.77.1: with a finger on the camera (rPPG running), record a short clip → Stop →
  play the shared .mp4 → confirm the audio pitch/tempo now matches what you heard live.
